1
00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:48,940
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:51,930
[Episode 23]

3
00:02:04,870 --> 00:02:06,870
Get some sleep after drinking this.

4
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:09,220
What about you?

5
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,250
You haven't been back for days.

6
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:14,880
I'll help tidy up your place a bit.

7
00:03:54,850 --> 00:04:02,820
[Quantum Entanglement]
[Parallel Universes]

8
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:23,940
Hello?

9
00:04:24,810 --> 00:04:26,070
Can't find something?

10
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:27,630
I can come over right away. I'm...

11
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:28,770
You're amazing.

12
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:30,100
My draft paper for calculating

13
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,040
plasma turbulence,

14
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,980
the one with the diagram

15
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:35,420
drawn in green pen on the back,

16
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:36,310
you actually put it

17
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:38,970
with last week's
differential geometry notes.

18
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:40,630
Your idea was spot on.

19
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,510
Also, how did you think of putting

20
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:46,040
Turing's biography and
Fermat's Last Theorem together?

21
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,430
Your logic is so clear.

22
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:51,270
It's much easier to find
than when I put them away myself.

23
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:54,130
I'll never have to worry about
losing things again.

24
00:04:54,310 --> 00:04:55,159
I...

25
00:04:55,360 --> 00:04:56,120
Jiang Yubai,

26
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:58,890
I think you're a genius at organizing.

27
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:00,500
Gosh,

28
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:03,120
this talent of yours
is so worth developing.

29
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,650
I just put them there randomly.

30
00:05:08,190 --> 00:05:09,920
As long as it's convenient for you.

31
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:11,500
It is, very convenient.

32
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,220
Are you home?

33
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:17,270
I...

34
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:22,870
Yes, I'm home.

35
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:23,750
Good.

36
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:25,620
Thank you.

37
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:26,820
Good night.

38
00:05:28,390 --> 00:05:29,070
Good night.

39
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:47,950
Duan.

40
00:05:49,870 --> 00:05:52,630
Agent Tang, you're finally here.

41
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:55,680
It's really hard to get
a meeting with you.

42
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:57,120
Your favorites,

43
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,430
I ordered them all for you.

44
00:05:58,430 --> 00:05:59,360
Go ahead and eat.

45
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,860
Mr. Duan, you're really spending today.

46
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:03,480
Isn't

47
00:06:04,190 --> 00:06:05,430
this very normal?

48
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,750
Why do I feel like

49
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:14,190
you're not here to eat,

50
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,680
but to vent?

51
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,830
Spit it out. What is it?

52
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:20,920
What do I have to rant about?

53
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:22,360
My mood

54
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:24,560
is as beautiful as the weather today.

55
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:27,060
I just suddenly wanted to have
a few drinks with you.

56
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:27,520
Come on.

57
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,620
All right.

58
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:33,510
Whoever stops drinking first
today is a coward.

59
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,960
That's the Tang I know.

60
00:06:37,070 --> 00:06:37,659
Come on.

61
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,430
Wait.

62
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:42,390
What?

63
00:06:42,390 --> 00:06:43,320
Get in the frame.

64
00:06:47,250 --> 00:06:47,980
Okay.

65
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:49,280
Do I look handsome?

66
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:50,040
Yes.

67
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:53,140
[Photos and Videos]

68
00:06:53,230 --> 00:06:53,650
[Tang]

69
00:06:53,670 --> 00:06:54,680
[Post]

70
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:57,810
Thank you, Mr. Duan, for the great treat.

71
00:06:59,070 --> 00:06:59,800
Let's drink.

72
00:06:59,830 --> 00:07:00,480
Cheers.

73
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,040
Bottoms up.

74
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:11,270
You really are a tough guy.

75
00:07:11,270 --> 00:07:12,510
No warm-up at all.

76
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,130
I'll join you.

77
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:21,700
Let's eat.

78
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,630
What is it? Tell me.

79
00:07:30,310 --> 00:07:31,920
Why can't I just have

80
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:34,360
some good food and drinks with you

81
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:37,080
to strengthen
our revolutionary friendship?

82
00:07:38,270 --> 00:07:39,360
Oh, come on.

83
00:07:39,720 --> 00:07:43,520
You've been in business for so long.
Surely you've made new friends.

84
00:07:43,950 --> 00:07:47,680
You look like you're drinking your
sorrows away in dreary weather.

85
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:49,180
No.

86
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:51,190
I just knew you were craving hotpot,

87
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:53,720
so I found a good restaurant
to share with you.

88
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:57,220
Wait a minute.

89
00:08:00,690 --> 00:08:01,540
Hello, Su Mo.

90
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:03,570
What's wrong? Aren't you at an audition?

91
00:08:03,570 --> 00:08:06,000
Tingting, it was supposed to be my turn,

92
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:08,940
but Mr. Yang brought
a few more people over.

93
00:08:09,660 --> 00:08:11,370
The casting director told me to wait here.

94
00:08:11,370 --> 00:08:13,130
It's been quite a while.

95
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,500
What should I do?

96
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:15,540
What happened?

97
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:17,450
Didn't you ask the people there?

98
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,300
I asked.

99
00:08:18,690 --> 00:08:20,820
But they didn't give me a clear answer.

100
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:23,570
Should I wait here

101
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:24,980
or go in and ask?

102
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:27,380
I'm coming over now.

103
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:28,660
Leave it to me.

104
00:08:36,130 --> 00:08:37,169
Sorry, Duan.

105
00:08:37,409 --> 00:08:39,270
I have an emergency and need to go.

106
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:41,980
It's your Su Mo again, isn't it?

107
00:08:42,169 --> 00:08:44,010
Why is he acting like a three-year-old

108
00:08:44,010 --> 00:08:45,870
and coming to you for everything?

109
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:47,320
No.

110
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:48,670
He's at an audition,

111
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:51,330
and they're keeping him waiting
for a long time.

112
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,480
Where's your professionalism?

113
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,740
He's asking others for a favor,

114
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:56,170
so waiting is to be expected.

115
00:08:56,170 --> 00:08:57,240
If he can't even stand this

116
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,960
and calls for backup to play the victim,

117
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,770
wouldn't that just make them
dislike him more?

118
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:02,940
It's not easy for him
to get an opportunity.

119
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,500
We can't just hand it over
to someone else.

120
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,010
Besides, this is my job.

121
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,120
I have to deal with it.

122
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:09,320
That is what you call professionalism.

123
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,210
I'm leaving.

124
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:21,620
I'm confiscating
these two bottles of liquor

125
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:23,950
so you don't drink yourself into a stupor.

126
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:32,370
Fine.

127
00:09:33,770 --> 00:09:36,100
Tang Tingting, you are really something.

128
00:10:10,290 --> 00:10:11,220
I've handled it.

129
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:16,160
We should drink our liquor together.

130
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:17,770
Fill it up.

131
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:38,600
You're here.

132
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,250
I came to see you,

133
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,270
and to bring you a toy.

134
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,830
A binary star system model?

135
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,100
Did you make it?

136
00:11:08,170 --> 00:11:09,600
It's so beautiful.

137
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:10,920
Do you like it?

138
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,800
It must have a lot of mechanisms.

139
00:11:24,790 --> 00:11:26,370
You put the emerald here?

140
00:11:30,030 --> 00:11:31,770
It's so pretty.

141
00:11:32,670 --> 00:11:34,130
It looks like an emerald.

142
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,170
Any stone in your hands

143
00:11:36,170 --> 00:11:37,550
would become a gem.

144
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,580
It must've been polished over time

145
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:44,480
to have such a perfect shape.

146
00:11:46,670 --> 00:11:47,360
For you.

147
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:51,790
Why give it to me?

148
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,550
Because I want to.

149
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,780
It's so beautiful.

150
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:01,580
It's like the center
of a binary star system.

151
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:05,630
Why don't you take a break
from studying this?

152
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:07,030
You can do it another day.

153
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:07,960
Um...

154
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,520
You haven't tasted my cooking yet, right?

155
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:12,650
I've had the vegetables you prepared.

156
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:13,670
That's perfect.

157
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,120
I must show you my skills.

158
00:12:15,130 --> 00:12:15,750
So...

159
00:12:16,400 --> 00:12:18,600
How about radish and beef brisket stew?

160
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,440
You can also think about

161
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:22,570
what you want to eat for the week ahead.

162
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:25,260
No need to go through all that trouble.

163
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,870
Cooking takes a long time.

164
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:28,330
We can just order takeout.

165
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:30,200
Takeout isn't as hygienic
as home-cooked food.

166
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:30,860
Let me do it.

167
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,000
Then what should I do?

168
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:36,390
Just find something to do.

169
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:38,350
I'll go buy groceries first.

170
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,030
What's up? Hungry?

171
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,620
No.

172
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,730
Are you okay?

173
00:13:28,750 --> 00:13:29,550
I'm fine.

174
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:41,130
Does it still hurt?

175
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,900
Your leg isn't healed yet.

176
00:13:46,030 --> 00:13:48,360
Don't wander around.
Go back and sit down.

177
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,360
Wait for me a bit longer.

178
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,490
It'll be ready soon.

179
00:15:21,350 --> 00:15:24,680
Why did you put the vegetables in
after turning off the heat?

180
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:28,000
Well, you have to

181
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,960
let it simmer
with the heat off for a while.

182
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:31,670
This is my secret recipe.

183
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,400
It tastes good only when
simmered this way.

184
00:15:54,910 --> 00:15:55,710
What's wrong?

185
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:57,550
I'm hungry.

186
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,720
Hungry?

187
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:01,820
It's almost done.

188
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:02,940
Let's eat.

189
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,640
Food is ready.

190
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,240
It smells so good.

191
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,580
It looks delicious.

192
00:16:15,630 --> 00:16:18,000
And it's my first time seeing two kinds

193
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,240
of radishes in this dish.

194
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,320
One is white radish,

195
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:21,780
and the other is carrot...

196
00:16:21,870 --> 00:16:22,500
shreds.

197
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,840
That's my secret recipe.

198
00:16:28,330 --> 00:16:29,150
Try it.

199
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:33,510
I know.

200
00:16:33,510 --> 00:16:35,310
You must have done it on purpose.

201
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:39,510
I saw you turn the heat down
really low just now.

202
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,840
You definitely wanted me to taste it
when I'm the hungriest

203
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,550
to enjoy your secret recipe.

204
00:16:46,030 --> 00:16:46,840
That's right.

205
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:50,550
You have to turn off the heat and

206
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:51,270
let it simmer

207
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:53,030
to make it taste good.

208
00:16:56,840 --> 00:16:57,480
Is it good?

209
00:16:58,790 --> 00:16:59,850
It's so delicious.

210
00:17:02,270 --> 00:17:03,270
I'll try the beef.

211
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,859
It's been stewed until it's so tender.

212
00:17:10,859 --> 00:17:12,450
That puzzle of yours

213
00:17:13,069 --> 00:17:14,569
is quite difficult, isn't it?

214
00:17:14,569 --> 00:17:15,790
It is quite hard.

215
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,400
Why don't you help me with it

216
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,730
after we finish eating?

217
00:17:19,510 --> 00:17:20,310
Okay.

218
00:17:33,350 --> 00:17:34,270
So good.

219
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:55,460
You must be sleepy.

220
00:17:57,350 --> 00:17:58,160
No, I'm not.

221
00:18:01,030 --> 00:18:01,830
Then

222
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:03,620
I'll head back first.

223
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,400
Thank you for today.

224
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:11,750
You stayed so late cooking for me.

225
00:18:13,270 --> 00:18:14,110
It's nothing.

226
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,030
How are you getting back?

227
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:16,880
It's so late.

228
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,330
The buses have probably stopped running.

229
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:20,960
I'll just take a taxi.

230
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:24,510
That's too expensive.

231
00:18:28,270 --> 00:18:29,480
I mean,

232
00:18:36,070 --> 00:18:37,870
why don't you stay here tonight?

233
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:42,350
That wouldn't be appropriate.

234
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:44,400
Your brother will scold me again
if he finds out.

235
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:45,730
Just don't let him know.

236
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:47,550
I'm mainly worried it's unsafe
for you to go home alone.

237
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:48,480
I'll get you a blanket so you can

238
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:50,680
sleep on the floor here. How about that?

239
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:28,600
[Hematology Department]

240
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:30,240
Zeqiu, what brings you here?

241
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:33,460
I came to process Lin Zhixia's discharge

242
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:34,810
and have a chat with you.

243
00:20:35,510 --> 00:20:37,350
You could've just called me to do it.

244
00:20:37,350 --> 00:20:39,400
There was no need to make a special trip.

245
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:41,070
Her hospitalization
has already troubled you a lot.

246
00:20:41,070 --> 00:20:42,070
I won't bother you

247
00:20:42,270 --> 00:20:43,800
with something so trivial.

248
00:20:44,350 --> 00:20:45,440
Don't be a stranger.

249
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:46,500
We are all friends.

250
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,580
How is Zhixia recovering?

251
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,200
Pretty well. She's recovering nicely.

252
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:54,590
Her leg still needs rest.

253
00:20:54,770 --> 00:20:55,830
Don't rush to walk.

254
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,580
Avoid secondary injury.

255
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:00,140
I'll remind her later.

256
00:21:02,590 --> 00:21:03,880
You've been working hard too.

257
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:04,720
You had to work

258
00:21:04,720 --> 00:21:06,180
and take care of a patient.

259
00:21:06,720 --> 00:21:07,400
It's not hard.

260
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,270
I've just been a bit busy lately.

261
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:12,060
At the hospital, I have your help.

262
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:13,030
As for Lin Zhixia,

263
00:21:13,030 --> 00:21:15,160
she has Jiang Yubai taking care of her.

264
00:21:22,310 --> 00:21:25,380
How are the two PhDs
I found for Zhixia last time?

265
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,590
If they're no good,

266
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:28,590
I can ask my mom to find someone else.

267
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:32,750
I understand what you mean.

268
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:33,550
But above all,

269
00:21:35,510 --> 00:21:37,050
Lin Zhixia said she doesn't need them.

270
00:21:37,050 --> 00:21:38,510
She can handle it herself.

271
00:21:42,310 --> 00:21:44,640
Doesn't she lack manpower and resources?

272
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:46,210
These two people

273
00:21:46,590 --> 00:21:48,030
should be of great help.

274
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:49,510
That's what I thought too.

275
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:51,830
I asked both you
and Jiang Yubai about this.

276
00:21:51,830 --> 00:21:53,380
I thought your method

277
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,830
was more effective

278
00:21:54,830 --> 00:21:55,880
and reliable.

279
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,400
But maybe Jiang Yubai

280
00:22:00,550 --> 00:22:02,350
understands Lin Zhixia better.

281
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,310
What did he say?

282
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,220
He said Lin Zhixia doesn't need help,

283
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,860
and she can do it on her own.

284
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:13,720
